{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-40687",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The given repeating decimal can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7.8\\overset{―}{7} & =7.877\\,7... \\\\  & =7.8+0.07+0.007+0.000\\,7+… \\\\  & =7.8+(\\frac{7}{100}+\\frac{7}{1\\,000}+\\frac{7}{10\\,000}+…).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe series in the parentheses is a geometric series with first term ${a}_{1}=\\frac{7}{100}$ and common ratio $r=\\frac{1}{10}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7.8\\overset{―}{7} & =7.8+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{1}{r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =7.8+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{7}{100}{(\\frac{1}{10})}^{n-1} \\\\  & =7.8+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{7\\cdot 10}{100}{(\\frac{1}{10})}^{n} \\\\  & =7.8+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{7}{10}{(\\frac{1}{10})}^{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
